<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="chest-for-protection-warrior-tank">Chest for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>The World Drop BoE <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=67143/icebone-hauberk">
<img alt="Icebone Hauberk" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raiddeathknight_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icebone Hauberk</span></a> is technically speaking the best chest piece before raids in Phase 1, but only so by a small margin that probably isn't worth spending any gold on in all honesty. The secondary stats are only mediocre, with a small amount of hit rating to reforge into mastery, and the socket bonus is awful, which makes this ilvl 359 epic barely an upgrade to ilvl 346 blues in this list. Unless it's dirt cheap on the Auction House, don't waste your gold and prefer the two next options on the list.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58101/chestplate-of-the-steadfast">
<img alt="Chestplate of the Steadfast" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_dungeonplate_c_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chestplate of the Steadfast</span></a> and the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56308/beautys-plate">
<img alt="Beauty's Plate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_dungeonplate_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Beauty's Plate</span></a> are almost identical so only spend the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> on the former if you are really unlucky and can't get the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=4926/blackrock-caverns">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Blackrock Caverns</span></a> <span class="icon-heroic"></span> one. They both come with high mastery and a defensive secondary stat making them perfect for tanks.<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=55060/elementium-deathplate">
<img alt="Elementium Deathplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Deathplate</span></a>, despite being a 359 epic, is barely worth mentioning as a 4th option because of its DPS-oriented stats and lack of gem socket, and probably not worth crafting unless money is no object. Unfortunately, the tank-oriented craft <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=55058/hardened-elementium-hauberk">
<img alt="Hardened Elementium Hauberk" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hardened Elementium Hauberk</span></a> is even worse, with mediocre secondary stats and a dreadful socket bonus. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Chest Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=74251/enchant-chest-greater-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Chest - Greater Stamina</span></a>
