<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-protection-warrior-tank">Trinkets for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>The <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=171/alchemy">
<img alt="Alchemy" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_alchemy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alchemy</span></a> exclusive <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58483/lifebound-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Lifebound Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_aspiration.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifebound Alchemist Stone</span></a> is technically speaking the best pre-raid trinket. However, its weaker profession perks compared to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_armorkit_17.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> entirely offset the benefits of this trinket so I don't recommend leveling this profession as a <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=1/warrior">
<img alt="Warrior" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a>. Moreover, there are no upgrades to the Alchemist stones in Cataclysm so this trinket is pretty ephemeral and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=171/alchemy">
<img alt="Alchemy" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_alchemy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alchemy</span></a> doesn't provide anything special for the rest of the expansion.<br/>In that same vein, the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=755/jewelcrafting">
<img alt="Jewelcrafting" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jewelcrafting</span></a> trinket <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52352/figurine-earthen-guardian">
<img alt="Figurine - Earthen Guardian" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_earthenmight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Figurine - Earthen Guardian</span></a> is also a great pickup before starting raids, and the perfect swap for physical encounters where the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62471/mirror-of-broken-images">
<img alt="Mirror of Broken Images" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_platnumdisks.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mirror of Broken Images</span></a> on-use loses a lot of value. But once again, the average profession perks of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=755/jewelcrafting">
<img alt="Jewelcrafting" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jewelcrafting</span></a> compared to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_armorkit_17.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> offset that gain entirely.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Now for the trinkets should you <i>actually</i> get.</b> <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56347/leaden-despair">
<img alt="Leaden Despair" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/quest_12252_icon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leaden Despair</span></a> is a fantastic trinket, with a big stack of stamina useful against every damage types, paired with arguably the best type of emergency procs <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92185">providing reliable damage mitigation when your health dips low</a>.<br/>Next on the list of must-haves for Phase 1 is the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62471/mirror-of-broken-images">
<img alt="Mirror of Broken Images" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_platnumdisks.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mirror of Broken Images</span></a>. This one might be a painful grind since it requires reaching Exalted with the <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1177/baradins-wardens">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Baradin's Wardens</span></a>/<wbr/>
<a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1178/hellscreams-reach">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Hellscream's Reach</span></a> PvP reputations via dailies and PvP events, and it might not be feasible before your first raid. However, the trinket is definitely worth the effort for its excellent on-use <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92222/image-of-immortality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Image of Immortality</span></a> providing high magic damage mitigation on a short cooldown, reminiscent of the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=50364/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img alt="Sindragosa's Flawless Fang" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a> from Wrath. Stamina in place of Mastery would have made this trinket perfect against magic damage, since our mastery <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=76857/critical-block">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_criticalblock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Critical Block</span></a> only affects physical damage. Block tanks get the short end of the stick once again.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56280/porcelain-crab">
<img alt="Porcelain Crab" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_purplecrab.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Porcelain Crab</span></a> is a good trinket to pair with <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56347/leaden-despair">
<img alt="Leaden Despair" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/quest_12252_icon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leaden Despair</span></a> until you reach Exalted with the <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1177/baradins-wardens">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Baradin's Wardens</span></a>/<wbr/>
<a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1178/hellscreams-reach">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Hellscream's Reach</span></a> factions to buy the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62471/mirror-of-broken-images">
<img alt="Mirror of Broken Images" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_platnumdisks.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mirror of Broken Images</span></a>. You can expect about a ~20% uptime of the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92175">mastery rating proc</a> <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92174/hardened-shell">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_shell_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hardened Shell</span></a>. However, the mastery from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62471/mirror-of-broken-images">
<img alt="Mirror of Broken Images" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_platnumdisks.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mirror of Broken Images</span></a> alone beats the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56280/porcelain-crab">
<img alt="Porcelain Crab" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_purplecrab.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Porcelain Crab</span></a> against all-physical incoming damage.<div class="pad"></div>
<table class="grid max-width">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td data-background="c1" style="width: 10%; max-width: 100%;">
<b>Rank</b></td>
<td data-background="c1" style="width: 25%; max-width: 100%;">
<b>Item</b></td>
<td data-background="c1" style="width: 20%; max-width: 100%;">
